WEBVTT

cue0062152
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.000
I want to thank the lady because because of the lady I was able to come today to Selehot. You know why? No pude dormir. Me levante temprano.

cue0062153
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.000
No, no, estoy bromeando.

cue0062154
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:33.820
Well, Jews, Judaism, the scripture, have contributed an enormous, enormous amount of ideas that revolutionized mankind.

cue0062155
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:38.440
Revolutionized the pagan, what I call pagan humanity.

cue0062156
00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:47.700
And one of the central ideas of the Hebrews is the idea of teshuba, repentance.

cue0062157
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.000
simply is something that belongs to the realm of science fiction.

cue0062158
00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:54.380
Teshuba.

cue0062159
00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.960
But Teshuba says like this, and I explain it,

cue0062160
00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:00.760
that if a person committed something that is wrong,

cue0062161
00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.600
or he, she feels that is wrong,

cue0062162
00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:08.740
somehow it's possible to repent,

cue0062163
00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:13.300
and by repenting, you change the past.

cue0062164
00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:17.620
It is as if the past never existed.

cue0062165
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.200
you did something wrong

cue0062166
00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.440
and so to speak

cue0062167
00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:23.680
you go back into time

cue0062168
00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.900
or rather God goes back into time

cue0062169
00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:27.660
and changes that

cue0062170
00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:30.240
that is a new idea

cue0062171
00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.340
because in the pagan humanity

cue0062172
00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:34.580
Plato, Aristotle

cue0062173
00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:35.420
etc

cue0062174
00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:37.300
if you do something

cue0062175
00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.660
first of all as a man

cue0062176
00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:42.160
you should not repent

cue0062177
00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:44.500
you should stick to your guns

cue0062178
00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:46.380
to repent

cue0062179
00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:47.400
to change your mind

cue0062180
00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.860
is a sign of weakness.

cue0062181
00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.200
And not only that

cue0062182
00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.060
it will not work,

cue0062183
00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.380
but there is this concept of fate,

cue0062184
00:01:57.260 --> 00:01:59.780
what in Latin they call it fatum,

cue0062185
00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.240
the decrees of the gods.

cue0062186
00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:04.960
And you cannot change that decree.

cue0062187
00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:08.240
And man is conceived as a kind of

cue0062188
00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:10.220
a clock.

cue0062189
00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:11.740
There is a mechanism in you.

cue0062190
00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:14.400
And this mechanism determines

cue0062191
00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.900
your behavior.

cue0062192
00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:18.860
and therefore you never can change it

cue0062193
00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:20.500
and you should not try to change it

cue0062194
00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:22.800
as a matter of fact if you know there's something very special

cue0062195
00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:24.800
about the Greeks is the concept of

cue0062196
00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:27.020
drama, what is drama?

cue0062197
00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:27.980
I don't know

cue0062198
00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.240
any other drama, Oedipus Rex,

cue0062199
00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:34.900
any other drama is always like this

cue0062200
00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:36.120
there is a fatum

cue0062201
00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:37.800
there is a decree

cue0062202
00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:40.180
issued by the God about an individual

cue0062203
00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:42.540
the individual

cue0062204
00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:44.940
tried to fight his destiny

cue0062205
00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:48.660
At the end, he fails.

cue0062206
00:02:50.400 --> 00:03:01.620
And peace, harmony, tranquility arrives at the moment that this individual recognizes that he cannot change his fate and accepts it.

cue0062207
00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:03.420
That's every single drama.

cue0062208
00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:04.360
Yes?

cue0062209
00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:07.560
Sophocles, Euripides, all of them, it's the same thing.

cue0062210
00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:12.780
In Judaism, we believe that we could change ourselves.

cue0062211
00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.060
that the destiny

cue0062212
00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:16.800
is up to us.

cue0062213
00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:19.200
And the central idea

cue0062214
00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.120
is that of teshuba,

cue0062215
00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:21.880
of repentance.

cue0062216
00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:24.300
We instituted

cue0062217
00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.580
a special kind of holidays

cue0062218
00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:28.740
that are devoted

cue0062219
00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:30.840
to the concept of teshuba.

cue0062220
00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:32.540
The holiday,

cue0062221
00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.240
it is Rosh ha-Shana,

cue0062222
00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:35.780
we'll speak about it in a minute,

cue0062223
00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:38.860
continues with

cue0062224
00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:40.480
'Aseret Yimei teshuba,

cue0062225
00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:43.540
special days that are dedicated

cue0062226
00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:46.800
or should be devoted to introspection

cue0062227
00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.420
and culminates in Yom Kippur.

cue0062228
00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:50.460
I will explain everything.

cue0062229
00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:53.580
But the first step is that this

cue0062230
00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:55.940
Rosh ha-Shana, Yom Kippur,

cue0062231
00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:57.220
is not a holiday.

cue0062232
00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.600
It's not a Yom Tob.

cue0062233
00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:03.060
We have only three.

cue0062234
00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:04.680
Yamim Tobim,

cue0062235
00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:08.880
Pesah, Shabu'ot, Sukkot.

cue0062236
00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:15.120
These are not called Yamim Tobim, but as a matter of fact, the opposite of Yamim Tobim.

cue0062237
00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:18.240
Yom Norayim, Days of Awe.

cue0062238
00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:22.580
And there's a difference between a Yom Tob and Yom Norah.

cue0062239
00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:31.980
Yom Tob, you celebrate a national, an event of national importance, national history.

cue0062240
00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:33.960
Something that happened in the past.

cue0062241
00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:36.280
the exodus from Egypt

cue0062242
00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:38.100
the pilgrimage

cue0062243
00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.560
40 years in the desert

cue0062244
00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:41.260
Matan Tora

cue0062245
00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:43.000
receiving the Tora in Shabu'ot

cue0062246
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.760
but in the days of Rosh ha-Shana

cue0062247
00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:46.480
in Yom Kippur

cue0062248
00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:49.800
you do not celebrate a past event

cue0062249
00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:51.440
but a current event

cue0062250
00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:54.020
in the days of Rosh ha-Shana

cue0062251
00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.160
Yom Kippur we are being judged

cue0062252
00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:57.940
it's something

cue0062253
00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.600
that is happening right now

cue0062254
00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:02.140
and because it's happening to us

cue0062255
00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:03.900
and we participate in this event

cue0062256
00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:07.260
And it is not a drama because it's up to us.

cue0062257
00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:12.040
We could tilt the events one way or the other.

cue0062258
00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:14.580
It's Yom Nora.

cue0062259
00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:21.880
It's a day of awe because the present is right now.

cue0062260
00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:25.220
The ball is in your hands.

cue0062261
00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:32.840
And if there is a mistake, if there is something wrong, you did it.

cue0062262
00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:34.160
Not the gods.

cue0062263
00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:36.700
Not a fatum, a decree.

cue0062264
00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:38.860
But it is you.

cue0062265
00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:40.580
Fine.

cue0062266
00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:43.480
The rabbis say

cue0062267
00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:46.740
that Rosh ha-Shana

cue0062268
00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:49.180
celebrates

cue0062269
00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:52.360
Adam.

cue0062270
00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:56.400
Adam is a special individual

cue0062271
00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:59.820
because he has intelligence.

cue0062272
00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:02.440
He can reason.

cue0062273
00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:13.180
he has conscious of himself if he did something wrong he's aware of it he

cue0062274
00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:20.920
could maintain a dialogue he could lie he could connive he could choose right

cue0062275
00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:29.240
he could choose wrong and Adam committed a sin we will explain in a minute, the sin.

cue0062276
00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:34.560
The sixth day, somehow God judges.

cue0062277
00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:46.140
The first time that a human being is judged and applies, gives a sentence and executes the sentence.

cue0062278
00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:52.060
And everything is in a period of time that is called the sixth day of creation.

cue0062279
00:06:52.060 --> 00:07:00.820
By the way, there is a common misunderstanding about the Jewish calendar.

cue0062280
00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:05.860
The Jewish calendar is the most difficult and most complex part of Jewish law, is the

cue0062281
00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:07.660
Kiddush ha-Hodesh.

cue0062282
00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:10.340
People don't know it, for whatever reason.

cue0062283
00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:18.620
And even fine rabbinic scholars are not aware that in the Jewish calendar begins the first

cue0062284
00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:20.280
day of the Jewish calendar,

cue0062285
00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.140
It's not Sunday.

cue0062286
00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:25.440
It's Shabbat.

cue0062287
00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:27.820
And I think it's very profound.

cue0062288
00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:29.380
It's terribly profound.

cue0062289
00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:32.560
It means that we begin

cue0062290
00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:34.740
chronological time

cue0062291
00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:37.780
post-Adam.

cue0062292
00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:39.480
Not pre-Adam.

cue0062293
00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:42.260
Post-Adam. After Adam

cue0062294
00:07:42.260 --> 00:07:44.060
sinned and came out of

cue0062295
00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:44.640
Gan Eden,

cue0062296
00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:48.240
Shabbat,

cue0062297
00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:52.720
then Shabbat is the first day of the Jewish calendar.

cue0062298
00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:55.440
Then we start measuring, not before.

cue0062299
00:07:58.180 --> 00:07:59.120
And if you pay attention,

cue0062300
00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:04.020
the days of Genesis are not coming as days.

cue0062301
00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:06.440
Because in Judaism, a day when it begins,

cue0062302
00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:08.780
when you begin, when you light the candles for Shabbat,

cue0062303
00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:10.900
the night begins at night.

cue0062304
00:08:11.540 --> 00:08:11.720
Yes?

cue0062305
00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:13.040
Kippur, at night.

cue0062306
00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:14.200
Rosh ha-Shana, at night.

cue0062307
00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:15.320
Every holiday at night.

cue0062308
00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:18.240
But those days begin when?

cue0062309
00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:24.620
in the morning yes how i'm sorry beginning at night, vayehi 'ereb and when it ends, vayehi boqer

cue0062310
00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:36.060
in the morning so it's not the regular day all right all right so remember adam is judged

cue0062311
00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:41.660
and therefore that dimension of humanity

cue0062312
00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:46.220
the consciousness that our acts

cue0062313
00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:50.040
are to be judged.

cue0062314
00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:51.900
Or in other words,

cue0062315
00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:54.000
that we are responsible for what we do.

cue0062316
00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:57.820
And that we have to face our maker.

cue0062317
00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:00.820
And our maker with issue.

cue0062318
00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:02.880
A judgment.

cue0062319
00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:04.820
And execute it.

cue0062320
00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:07.800
That complex idea

cue0062321
00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:10.700
is what makes a human a human.

cue0062322
00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:12.940
Therefore, Adam

cue0062323
00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:14.800
is the person

cue0062324
00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:17.300
who is conscious of his acts,

cue0062325
00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:21.400
he has the possibility therefore of sinning

cue0062326
00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:22.660
because he could choose

cue0062327
00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:25.140
he is aware that he has to render

cue0062328
00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:26.960
account in front of his maker

cue0062329
00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:29.820
and he accepts the judgment

cue0062330
00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:32.140
and this is

cue0062331
00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:33.380
Rosh ha-Shana.

cue0062332
00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:35.200
We shall continue

cue0062333
00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:38.120
but before let me explain you

cue0062334
00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:39.340
what does it mean

cue0062335
00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:40.620
to make the Teshuba

cue0062336
00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:43.600
and what is the nature of the first sin

cue0062337
00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:47.520
what was the sin

cue0062338
00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:50.340
the following explanation

cue0062339
00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:51.000
is not mine

cue0062340
00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:51.540
this comes from

cue0062341
00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:52.180
Rabbi Haim Palachi, Alav ha-Shalom

cue0062342
00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:53.540
one of the great Hakhamim

cue0062343
00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:54.560
from Izmir

cue0062344
00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:55.840
about 200 years ago.

cue0062345
00:09:55.840 --> 00:10:00.320
God asked Adam

cue0062346
00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:03.320
what did you do?

cue0062347
00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:07.040
and Adam says

cue0062348
00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:11.640
ha-isha asher natata 'imadi. it is not my fault,

cue0062349
00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:13.480
it is the woman

cue0062350
00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:15.160
she made me do it.

cue0062351
00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:18.960
Therefore incidentally

cue0062352
00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:21.480
it's not only that it's not my fault

cue0062353
00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:24.060
it's your fault God

cue0062354
00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:25.980
because you gave me this woman

cue0062355
00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:27.700
I didn't choose her

cue0062356
00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:28.340
alright

cue0062357
00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:29.860
it's your fault.

cue0062358
00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:34.100
God asked Eve,

cue0062359
00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:36.920
the snake.

cue0062360
00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:40.680
Here comes something very profound

cue0062361
00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:42.760
the real sin

cue0062362
00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:44.240
Is not a sin.

cue0062363
00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:50.560
The real sin is when an individual refuses to accept responsibility

cue0062364
00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:55.300
and blames somebody else for his or her misfortune.

cue0062365
00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:57.320
That is the sin.

cue0062366
00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:01.900
The first sin, the fruit, is only an incident.

cue0062367
00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:04.260
It's the marginality of the sin.

cue0062368
00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:08.420
When you cannot accept responsibility,

cue0062369
00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:10.640
where all of your flaws

cue0062370
00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:11.720
are the result.

cue0062371
00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:13.620
Your parents didn't educate you.

cue0062372
00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:16.740
Your sister, your brother-in-law,

cue0062373
00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:18.300
the neighbors,

cue0062374
00:11:18.980 --> 00:11:19.940
the school system,

cue0062375
00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:22.140
the Rabbi, of course.

cue0062376
00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:24.500
Yes. Especially the one who came to lecture

cue0062377
00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:26.800
to this. He made me do it.

cue0062378
00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:27.340
Alright?

cue0062379
00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:30.340
My wife, yes?

cue0062380
00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:32.260
Except,

cue0062381
00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:33.040
except,

cue0062382
00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:36.440
except myself.

cue0062383
00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:38.340
And here

cue0062384
00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:40.240
you come to a simple understanding.

cue0062385
00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:43.200
repentance

cue0062386
00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:46.280
permeates the whole Scripture.

cue0062387
00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:48.460
There's only

cue0062388
00:11:48.460 --> 00:11:49.480
one case

cue0062389
00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:52.480
in history in which

cue0062390
00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:54.660
repentance is not offered as an option.

cue0062391
00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:56.360
This is with Adam.

cue0062392
00:11:57.260 --> 00:11:58.180
God didn't say to Adam,

cue0062393
00:11:58.180 --> 00:11:59.360
why don't you make Teshuba?

cue0062394
00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:00.560
He didn't say this.

cue0062395
00:12:02.060 --> 00:12:03.980
And the reason is very simple.

cue0062396
00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:05.780
If you

cue0062397
00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:08.540
do not accept responsibility

cue0062398
00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:11.940
you are out of teshuba

cue0062399
00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:14.160
now I

cue0062400
00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:15.540
explain this a little bit more, and I say like this:

cue0062401
00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:20.140
the expulsion

cue0062402
00:12:20.140 --> 00:12:20.800
from Gan Eden

cue0062403
00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:24.220
the

cue0062404
00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:24.980
transformation

cue0062405
00:12:24.980 --> 00:12:28.140
from Gan Eden into something

cue0062406
